      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KARMA QUEEN (9) finds the maiden win elusive but it certainly hasn't been without trying. Could only manage a midfield finish last time in the slop at Murray Bridge when well found but her two runs prior were rippers. Can break through this time. IT'S A SOLID DEEL (5) returned last time with a solid third at this track over 1200m. Is sure to have come on from that and rates the main danger. IF YOU DON'T MIND (4) has been thereabouts in his last three and should be at his peak fitness now. Is yet to find a minor spot but is drawn well here and keeps the 2kg claimer. Ready to play a more significant role. KOHALA (6) often leaves himself with too much ground to bridge. Has had plenty of cracks to break through but has peaks littered through his form that can stand up in this. SIR AALI (8) opened the campaign in more encouraging fashion than what he's shown of late. Keeping safe off a freshen.",
